  "name": "Oyster Kasavu",
  "tagline": "A kasavu band woven in bronze",
  "idea": "Replaces champagne-smoke, which was a third Ink Smoke centred classic with a Playfair headline — smoked-champagne, charcoal-chandelier and shashtipoorthi-smoke already hold that exact ground, recipe and register. This takes the one shape nothing else in the formal set uses: a kasavu border in bronze instead of gold, for the Kerala Christian house that wears the same mundu as its Hindu neighbours. Two heavy horizontal bands survive the squint test outright, foil is off because a highlight travelling across a pale bronze band would read as a swatch, and Cinzel sits at 0.9 rather than the usual 0.85 so the names clear 46px.",
